            "Peak sun hours compress a day's variable irradiation into equivalent full-sun hours - 5 PSH means the day delivered 5 kWh per square metre however it was distributed. Multiplying the array's STC rating by PSH gives the ideal yield; the derate stack then charges reality: cells lose roughly 0.4%/C above 25 C, dust and shading take a few percent, wiring and inverter conversion more, and module mismatch and degradation the rest - a 0.75 system factor is a honest planning number in hot dusty climates. Off-grid design repeats the calculation for the worst month, not the annual average, because the battery and generator must survive December's irradiation, not July's.",
